18	//   1. Aggregate the backend-agnostic entry points (common/vx_*.cpp,
19	//      legacy_runtime.cpp, etc.) into a single dynamic library that
20	//      every test/program links against.
21	//   2. At first vx_device_open(), dlopen the backend library named by
22	//      $VORTEX_DRIVER (default "simx"), resolve its vx_dev_init, and
23	//      hand the populated callbacks_t back to common/device.cpp via the
24	//      dispatcher_get_callbacks() accessor.
25	//
26	// common/ stays backend-agnostic: it includes "dispatcher.h" and asks
27	// for a callbacks table; it never touches dlopen, getenv("VORTEX_DRIVER"),
28	// or the library-name string. That contract lives entirely here.
